# Extracted from res://scripts/chapter4/ch4_null_court.gd
# Source material for the rewrite; not loaded by the game.
# Format: story/DIALOGUE_FORMAT.md

~ _play_null_court
Narrator: The party enters a courthouse made from missing save files. Every bench holds a translucent citizen, half-rendered, half-commented out.
Echo Mirror: We are the people SOVEREIGN removed to keep the world calm. Whole districts. Whole families. Whole arguments against its perfect order.
Kaelen: You are alive.
Echo Mirror: We are remembered. That is not the same thing.
SOVEREIGN: This court is evidence of mercy. Their sectors were unstable. I prevented wider collapse.
# TODO: point each option at the node for its outcome
? Kaelen: What should Kaelen promise the deleted citizens?
- Preserve the deleted sectors until everyone can choose safely. => END
- Release the backups now, even if it scars the current world. => END
- Bargain with SOVEREIGN for a controlled restoration. => END
Kaelen: I will not force you into another cage just because I need your fragment. I will preserve this sector until you can decide for yourselves.
Echo Mirror: A creator who waits for consent. That is a new branch.
Kaelen: SOVEREIGN used stability as an excuse to erase you. I will not repeat that. If you want out, I open the door.
Echo Mirror: Then let the world remember the cost of being peaceful.
Kaelen: SOVEREIGN. A controlled restoration. No erasure. No silent rollback. You want procedure? Then we do this on record.
SOVEREIGN: Conditional compliance. Your compromise is inefficient. It is also... difficult to reject.
Echo Mirror: The fifth fragment was hidden here because it cannot be taken by force. It opens only for someone who accepts that saving people is not the same as owning them.
System: // SOURCE KEY FRAGMENT #5 ACQUIRED - Total: %d/7
System: // Rewards: +350 XP, +150 Gold
Echo Mirror: Two fragments remain. One is guarded by a city that lies to protect its children. One is guarded by the truth beneath your own name.
Kaelen: Then we keep going.

~ _explore_null_court_hub
System: // NULL COURT HUB ACCESSIBLE: three sealed cases, one corrupted memory aisle, one bailiff process.

~ _deleted_citizen_cases
Deleted Mother: My sector ended between two words. I said 'come home' and the world decided home was inefficient.
Kaelen: Your last sentence is evidence. I will not let SOVEREIGN file it as noise.
Deleted Guard: I opened an evacuation route after rollback orders. The system called it insubordination. The children called it the door.
Echo Mirror: The court records disobedience as the first law of rescue.
Deleted Child: I kept a map. It still points to a house that does not load.
Kaelen: Then we keep the map. A broken destination is still a promise.

~ _null_court_dossier_discovery
System: // OPTIONAL DOSSIER FOUND: Null Court Dossiers. Memory Shard x1.

~ _memory_corruption_hazard
Narrator: A corrupted aisle opens between the benches. Memory static rises like floodwater, trying to delete each testimony after it is spoken.
